  "result": "All eight tests pass, across both test files.\n\nChanges in `ratelimit/limiter.py`:\n\n- **Added `remaining(key, now)`.** It evicts expired timestamps for the key and returns the per-key limit minus the calls still in the window, floored at zero. It reads existing state only and never creates a log for an unknown key.\n- **Added `reset(key)`.** It drops the key's call log so the next burst starts fresh.\n- **Added `set_limit(key, limit)`.** It stores a per-key override in a new dictionary that `allow` and `remaining` consult before falling back to the constructor limit. The window is unchanged. Limits below one are rejected, matching the constructor.\n- **Factored out eviction** into a shared helper so all three read paths apply the same inclusive boundary rule.\n\nOne judgment call: `reset` clears usage but keeps any per-key limit override, since the override is configuration rather than call history. If you want `reset` to also drop the override, it is a one-line change.",
